An original game. No names, characters, maps, models, sounds or code from
any other game or franchise.

Art and sound
- Models come from the per-style asset library
  (@netnetcapital/asset-library): CC0 1.0 models by Kenney (Car Kit: the
  karts and trucks; Nature Kit: trees; City Kit Commercial: buildings;
  Space Kit: barrels) and Quaternius
  (via Poly Pizza: the coin), each pack listed with its
  source URL and licence verification in that package's NOTICE and
  manifest/packs.json. The files are fetched and built, never committed
  here; the build copies only the models this game uses.
- The road, kerbs, barriers, boost pads, the start line and the fallback
  kart (client/scene.ts) are generated from three.js primitives; all textures
  are drawn on a canvas at load. Sounds are the library's CC0 samples with
  WebAudio-synthesized fallbacks (client/audio.ts).

Dependencies (unmodified, via npm)
- three.js 0.186.1 (https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js), MIT.
- @netnetcapital/engine and @netnetcapital/engine-sim (this repository);
  see their NOTICE files (bitECS MPL-2.0, Rapier Apache-2.0, Colyseus MIT,
  zod MIT).

Patterns (ideas only)
- The kart racing genre's general mechanics (laps, drifting to charge a
  boost, boost pads, coins, a grid of rivals). Mechanics, not expression;
  no track, vehicle, character or text was copied from any game.
- Arcade vehicle handling (forward and sideways velocity, grip, drift) as
  described in common public write-ups on arcade car physics. Implemented
  from scratch in engine-sim src/kart.ts.
